# This repo IS the deploy root — anything committed here is served publicly
# (GitHub Pages serves every file in the branch, and directory listings are
# available for folders with no index). Local working files that contain real
# owner/tenant data must therefore never be committed, even by accident.

# Generated/exported owner statements and reports. The app builds these
# client-side and hands them straight to the browser's download — none of them
# belong in the repo.
statement/
statements/
*.pdf

# Playwright, installed on demand for scripts/smoke-test.mjs. There is
# deliberately no package.json — `npm install --no-save playwright` leaves this
# directory behind, and since GitHub Pages serves everything in the branch,
# committing it would publish ~19 MB of browser tooling to the live site.
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# Local scratch and editor/OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.local
*.log
.vscode/
.idea/

# Secrets — CONFIG in index.html deliberately carries only the publishable
# anon key; a service-role key must never land in a served file.
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
